@* What a page's or a table's old place shows while it is in a window of its own (the owner, 2026-11-27: "that
   grid or page should go blank on the original app with a reattach button in the pane to bring it back"): the
   shared empty state, one sentence and two buttons. Reattach closes its window and shows it here again where it
   is now; Show window brings its window to the front. *@
@inject PopOuts PopOuts

<div class="empty-state pop-out-placeholder" role="status" data-pop-out="@Entry.Key">
    <Icon Name="popout" />
    <p>@Entry.Placeholder</p>
    <div class="empty-state-actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn primary pop-out-reattach" @onclick="() => PopOuts.ReattachAsync(Entry.Key)"><Icon Name="popin" /> Reattach</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn pop-out-show" @onclick="() => PopOuts.ShowAsync(Entry.Key)"><Icon Name="popout" /> Show window</button>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>What is in a window of its own.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public PopOutEntry Entry { get; set; } = default!;
}
